---
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="UTF-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="256x256" href="/favicon-original-tent-close.png?v=8" />
		<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png?v=8" />
		<title>I don’t have a plan — Olivia Fjord Sloth</title>
		<meta name="description" content="A personal essay about leaving a job, travelling to Syria and choosing uncertainty over a fixed plan." />
	</head>

	<body>
		<SiteHeader />

		<main>
			<section class="hero">
				<img src="/stories/facebook.webp" alt="Olivia Fjord Sloth on a mountain trail" decoding="async" />

				<div class="hero-text">
					<p class="category">PERSONAL ESSAY</p>

					<h1>I don’t have<br />a plan</h1>

					<p class="subtitle">
						In a few weeks, I’m leaving my job and flying to Syria
						on a one-way ticket.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<article>
				<p>
					I’ve been struggling with how to tell this story.
				</p>

				<p>
					It’s easier to tell a story when you have a plan.
				</p>

				<p>
					The problem is that I don’t.
				</p>

				<p>
					I’ve realised that I’m not even sure what I’m afraid of anymore.
				</p>

				<p>
					Is it the discomfort of not having a plan? Or is it because I don’t
					have a good answer when people ask me why I’m doing this?
				</p>

				<p>
					In a few weeks, I’m flying to Syria on a one-way ticket. I’ve quit
					my job, rented out my apartment and, for the first time in a very
					long time, I don’t really know what comes next.
				</p>

				<p>
					Normally, when I set off on an adventure, I know what success looks
					like. I know what mountain I’m climbing or what route I’m walking.
					There’s always a clear objective.
				</p>

				<p>
					I’ve been to Syria three times before, and when I left the last time,
					I knew it wasn’t the end. There are still people I want to see again,
					places I haven’t explored and stories I’m curious about.
				</p>

				<p>
					What scares me isn’t leaving a specific job. It’s stepping away from
					a career I’ve spent years building.
				</p>

				<p>
					I love programming, solving problems and the satisfaction of finally
					understanding something that seemed impossible just a few hours
					earlier. Technology moves fast, and I sometimes wonder whether
					there’ll still be a place for me when I come back.
				</p>

				<p>
					I don’t know what’s waiting for me in Syria.
				</p>

				<p>
					What I do know is that the country has given me far more than I ever
					expected. I’ve learned so much from the people I’ve met, and I’ve
					been humbled by how many Syrians have told me that they appreciate
					the way I share their country.
				</p>

				<p>
					I never expected either of those things, but they’ve made it
					impossible for me to ignore the feeling that I need to go back.
				</p>

				<p>
					I’m not fearless.
				</p>

				<p>
					But I know I’ll spend far more time wondering what would have
					happened if I stayed home than I ever will regret that I tried.
				</p>

				<p>
					Over the next few months, I want to write about what happens when
					you step away from a life you’ve spent years building without
					knowing exactly what you’re moving towards.
				</p>

				<p>
					About Syria, of course. But also about uncertainty, doubt, work,
					identity, responsibility and the strange feeling of choosing a path
					before you know where it leads.
				</p>
                <figure class="story-image">
					<img src="/stories/tent.webp" alt="Tent spot" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
				</figure>
			</article>

			<div class="back">
				<a href="/stories">← Back to stories</a>
			</div>
		</main>
		<SiteFooter />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	* {
		box-sizing: border-box;
	}

	html,
	body {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		background: #f4f1ea;
		color: #171717;
	}

	body {
		font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
	}

	a {
		color: inherit;
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	header {
		padding: 30px 48px;
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.name {
		font-size: 22px;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
	}

	nav {
		display: flex;
		gap: 32px;
	}

	nav a {
		font-size: 15px;
	}

	.hero {
		position: relative;
		width: 100%;
		height: min(78vh, 850px);
		overflow: hidden;
	}

	.hero img {
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
	}

	.hero::after {
		content: "";
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0;
		background: linear-gradient(
			90deg,
			rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.38) 0%,
			rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.10) 60%,
			rgba(0, 0, 0, 0) 100%
		);
	}

	.hero-text {
		position: absolute;
		z-index: 2;
		left: 8%;
		top: 45%;
		transform: translateY(-50%);
		max-width: 850px;
		color: #f4f1ea;
	}

	.category {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 12px;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.18em;
	}

	.hero-text h1 {
		margin: 15px 0 25px;
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: clamp(60px, 7vw, 115px);
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 0.9;
		letter-spacing: -0.04em;
	}

	.hero-text .subtitle {
		max-width: 650px;
		margin: 0;
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: clamp(20px, 2vw, 30px);
		line-height: 1.3;
	}

	article {
		max-width: 700px;
		margin: 90px auto 0;
		padding: 0 30px;

		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: 21px;
		line-height: 1.75;
	}

	article p {
		margin: 0 0 34px;
	}

	.back {
		max-width: 700px;
		margin: 90px auto 120px;
		padding: 35px 30px 0;
		border-top: 1px solid #bbb;
		font-size: 14px;
	}
    .story-image {
        margin: 60px 0;
    }

    .story-image img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: auto;
    }
	@media (max-width: 700px) {
		header {
			padding: 24px 20px;
		}

		.name {
			font-size: 17px;
		}

		nav {
			gap: 14px;
		}

		nav a {
			font-size: 13px;
		}

		.hero {
			height: 72vh;
		}

		.hero-text {
			left: 24px;
			right: 24px;
			top: 46%;
		}

		.hero-text h1 {
			font-size: 54px;
		}

		.hero-text .subtitle {
			font-size: 20px;
		}

		article {
			margin-top: 60px;
			padding: 0 24px;
			font-size: 19px;
			line-height: 1.7;
		}

		.back {
			padding-left: 24px;
			padding-right: 24px;
		}
	}
</style>
